  "source_basis": {
    "profile": "Fresh IP-only post-path profile at baseline81ad419a7 pins Core1ce/CLId606/input9331 and directly samples global SlugConfiguration::hash13.18% self. Shared String/SipHasher symbols are not assigned to configuration, nor is all globalConfigHash work assigned to these wrappers.",
    "natural_owners": "Analysis ConfiguredTargetKey and other DICE keys retain ConfigurationKey; analysis/dice source is actually app/slug_analysis_v2/src/dice.rs:3209\u20133240, which constructs command registration natural keys from immutable configuration. StableKey hashes flow through FunctionEvaluationOwner/NativeFunctionOwner to StarlarkHasher, with separate complete equality.",
    "strong_domains": "Analysis artifact_owner uses complete_identity_bytes; Core FileWrite identity writes canonical configuration bytes. Neither wrapper implements StrongHash. Global SlugConfiguration Hash/StrongHash and finish_configuration remain byte-exact.",
    "donor": "Concept/test only: Buck2 Hashed separates operational Hash from full Eq and StrongHash. No donor code imported; reuse the pre-existing projection instead of adding a cached scalar or wrapping/recomputing at each fresh constructor."
  },
  "design": {
    "approval": "Independent design/source/ordinary and final evidence review ACCEPT.",
    "threshold_before_measurement": "For64 fresh keys from one real immutable341-option configuration, configuration-slot hashing must be exactly32 bytes per call including fresh construction; preserve full structural and persisted identities. This fixed byte-work threshold is separate from wall-time/RSS.",
    "implementation": "Analysis Slug arm hashes original mem::discriminant plus raw projection32; Legacy delegates original identity.hash. Loading hashes original workspace, raw projection32, original family. Both manual impls exhaustively destructure original key fields.",
    "ownership_memory": "Zero new retained field/allocation/cache/interner/constructor hashing/owner. Existing Arc/Allocative layouts, positive accounting and last-owner lifetimes are unchanged; no stack/RSS or whole-command memory claim.",
    "scope": "Operational buckets only. Full Eq resolves collisions, including configured/function-owner identities; no digest-only equality, publication permission or canonical/content/persisted hash authority. Starlark/DICE docs clarify this distinction."
  },
